// The key exported functions/classes/types and their purposes are:
// - sys/arch/rp2040/dev/usb.c: Provides the core architecture and device information.
// - sys/arch/rp2040/dev/usb.c: Handles device configuration and boot sequence.
// - sys/arch/rp2040/dev/flash.c: Manages flash memory operations and bootloader interactions.
// - sys/arch/rp2040/dev/usb.c: Contains driver-specific code and reset logic.
// - sys/arch/rp2040/dev/usb.c: Includes driver-specific APIs and compatibility information.

// The important dependencies are:
// - sys/param.h: Provides access to device parameters and configuration.
// - sys/conf.h: Contains device configuration settings and options.
// - sys/systm.h: Offers system-level information about the SDK and drivers.
// - sys/user.h: Provides user interface and control information.
// - sys/ioctl.h: Offers low-level I/O operations and device control functions.
// - sys/tty.h: Contains I/O and communication interfaces for the SDK.
// - sys/config.h: Provides device configuration data and settings.
// - sys/configure.h: Handles configuration updates and changes.
// - sys/configure_desktop.h: Manages device startup and bootloader behavior.
// - sys/configure_rdr.h: Manages device register and settings.
// - sys/config_rdr.h: Provides device status and bootloader state information.
// - sys/usb_ms_os_20_desc: Handles the MS OS 2.0 descriptor set and its properties.
// - sys/usb_ms_os_20_descriptor.h: Provides the MS OS 2.0 descriptor set information.
// - usb_bos_desc: Manages the BOS descriptor and its properties.
// - usb_ms_os_20_desc: Manages the MS OS 20 descriptor set and its capabilities.
// - usb_ms_os_20_callback: Handles callbacks and interrupts related to the MS OS 20.
// - usb_ep0_stall: Manages the EP0 IN stall and its effects on the bootloader.
// - usb_ep0_send: Manages the EP0 IN reply and its effects on the bootloader.
// - usb_ep0_ack: Manages the EP0 OUT reply and its effects on the bootloader.
// - usb_configure: Configures the SDK and its settings.
// - usb_reset_to_bootsel: Resets the endpoints based on the configuration settings.
// - usb_reset_to_flash: Resets the flash memory based on the configuration settings.
// - usb_setup: Configures the SDK and its settings.
// - usb_ep0_ack: Actions performed when the EP0 IN reply is acknowledged.
// - usb_ep0_expect_status: Actions performed when the EP0 OUT status is acknowledged.
// - usb_string_desc: Handles string-related operations and responses.
// - usb_configure: Configures the SDK and its settings.
// - usb_rm_reset: Resets the TIMERAWL interrupt.
// - usb_rdr: Resets the USB debugger and its flags.
// - usb_usb_tx_ring: Manages the USB TX ring and its behavior.
// - usb_usb_usb: Manages the USB debugger and its interrupts.
